**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests`

**How to implement.** Opening a kit bumps the kit history, and the 16-entry `recent.json` list goes (001 §F 'Storage': the history replaces the 16-entry recent.json list, and the existing pure MRU logic `RecentFiles.bump` is REUSED and extended over a clock provider; 001 §R 'The 16-entry recent.json list, replaced by the kit history (bump reused)'; .spec-md §0.1, §6 'History MRU', §7: the kit history starts empty). (1) The move. `RecentFiles.bump` (`RecentFiles.fs:RecentFiles.bump`: drop any case-insensitive duplicate, put the new one first, truncate to `maxRecent`) moves into `KitHistory` (step 164) as `member this.bump (limit : KitHistoryLimit) (clock : ClockProvider) (folder : KitFolder) (kitFile : KitFile) : KitHistory`, generalised from file names to entries: the entry matching `folder` (step 164's folder identity) is removed; a new entry `{ folder = folder; kitId = kitFile.id; name = kitFile.name; lastOpened = clock.now (); star = <the removed entry's star, or UnstarredKit when there was none> }` is put first; then `evict limit` (step 164) runs where the truncation ran. The clock is read once. A reopened kit thus keeps its star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and time; the cap drops the oldest unstarred kit and never a star, the just-opened kit included when every other kit is starred, because the limit is the history's ceiling (001 §F 'up to `KitHistoryLimit`'). Its doc cites spec 0050 S5.1. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:35`): `bump` moved in (1), and `maxRecent`, `prefsPath`, `loadRecent` and `FileName.pushRecent` are superseded by step 168's store, which keeps `kit-history.json` where `recent.json` was; nothing in the product called them. The comment above that `<Compile>` line keeps only words true of the line that now follows it and loses every word about recent files; nothing is added. (3) The docs that point at the deleted store point at the kit history instead, in no more words: `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs`' module doc (`UserEnvironment.fs:7-8`) and `EnvironmentSettings`' doc (`:227-228`) say that recently opened kits are kept by the kit history (`KitHistoryProxy`, spec 0050 S5.1), not here; `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs`' `sample` doc (`EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:49-51`) and its old-file section comment (`:373-375`) say the same. No comment anywhere names the deleted module or its file, step 164's docs included. Neither file changes behaviour, and the old-environment facts keep their assertions. (4) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj:49`). Its one fact (step 159), `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent`, moves to `KitHistoryTests` as `bump puts the opened kit first, matches its folder in any case and evicts beyond the limit`, over a clock stepping one second per call and a kit file per folder (`KitFile.create`, step 122): bumping `C:\kits\b` onto a history holding `C:\kits\a` lists `b` then `a`; bumping `C:\KITS\A` then lists `C:\KITS\A` then `b`, with no duplicate; and twenty distinct `C:\kits\f<i>` bumped from `KitHistory.empty` under `KitHistoryLimit 16` leave 16 entries, headed by `f20` and ending with `f5`. `KitHistoryTests` also gains `bump keeps a reopened kit's star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and last open`: a starred `C:/kits/a` named `Old`, bumped as `C:/KITS/A` with a kit file of another id named `New`, is first, starred, named `New`, with the new id, the folder text `C:/KITS/A` and the clock's time, and no other entry of that folder is left. `a bump over the limit drops the oldest unstarred kit and keeps every star`: under `KitHistoryLimit 3`, a history of unstarred `u2` (12:03), unstarred `u1` (12:02) and starred `s` (12:01), bumped with a new `n`, holds `n`, `u2` and `s`: `u1` is dropped and the older star is kept. `a bump into a full starred history never drops a star`: under `KitHistoryLimit 3`, a history of three starred kits bumped with a new `n` equals those three starred kits unchanged, and bumping the last of them instead puts it first, still starred, with all three kept. Afterwards `git grep -n -F -e RecentFiles -e recent.json -e maxRecent -e pushRecent -e loadRecent -e prefsPath -- Berreman/` finds nothing, which S5.2 onward asserts.

**Acceptance.** After `bump` moves into the kit history, `KitHistory.bump` MUST put the opened kit first with its star kept and evict the oldest unstarred kit over the limit, and `git grep -n -F -e RecentFiles -e recent.json -e maxRecent -e pushRecent -e loadRecent -e prefsPath -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `bump puts the opened kit first, matches its folder in any case and evicts beyond the limit` (moved from HistoryTests), `bump keeps a reopened kit's star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and last open`, `a bump over the limit drops the oldest unstarred kit and keeps every star` and `a bump into a full starred history never drops a star`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.
